WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.590
I know your pain, I know you're hurt.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:08.550
We had an election that was stolen from us,

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.690
it was a landslide election,

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:14.680
and everyone knows it especially the other side,

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.230
but you have to go home now.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:20.300
Donald Trump's response to last week's attack on the US Capitol led Twitter

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.580
to permanently ban him from its platform,

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.250
and Facebook and YouTube closed his accounts

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.030
on the grounds that he had used their platforms to incite violence.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.440
Next Apple and Google banned the Twitter competitor, Parler,

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.660
from its app stores on the grounds that

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.910
the perpetrators of last week's attack used it to coordinate,

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:42.170
and because the service doesn't engage in adequate content moderation.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:46.390
Then Amazon which owns about a third of the global cloud storage market,

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:49.170
evicted Parler from its cloud hosting service

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.990
taking the site down entirely.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:53.760
These decisions drew a ferocious reaction,

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.090
both for and against,

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.210
from people of all political stripes.

00:00:57.210 --> 00:01:01.867
For better or worse, as Edward Snowden put it after Trump was kicked off Twitter,

00:01:01.867 --> 00:01:04.160
this will be remembered as a turning point

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:07.048
in the battle for control over digital speech.

00:01:07.048 --> 00:01:11.040
It is stunning to watch now as every war on terror rhetorical tactic

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.720
to justify civil liberties erosions is now being invoked in the name of combating Trumpism,"

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.150
wrote Glenn Greenwald.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.730
So how should those who value a free and open society

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:24.990
feel about the deplatforming of the commander-in-chief?

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.540
The ongoing purge of many of his supporters

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:32.270
and repression of discussion of 2020 election voter fraud claims.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:36.415
Twitter is a private company and CEO Jack Dorsey's capacity

00:01:36.415 --> 00:01:39.240
to evict even the president of the United States,

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.115
is something worth valuing.

00:01:41.115 --> 00:01:42.820
But what if the network power

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.910
of a handful of Silicon Valley giants,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.570
is so great that there's nowhere else to turn?

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:50.790
And are Facebook, Twitter, and Google acting independently

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.620
or bending to the will of Congress

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.120
at a time when tech has been so deeply politicized?

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:59.740
The takeaway from the great deplatforming of 2021 is that

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.070
we need now more than ever an open digital commons

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:07.191
where individuals can maintain ownership of their own identities

00:02:07.191 --> 00:02:10.500
and speech is highly resistant to political pressure.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.900
Decentralized networks are vital to protecting open discourse

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:16.060
not only from Twitter, Facebook, and Google

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:19.790
but from Ted Cruz, Joe Biden, Josh Hawley, or Kamala Harris,

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:21.500
which is where the real power lies

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.530
to stomp on the free speech rights of American citizens.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:27.100
It's easy to forget that not long ago,

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.930
Twitter's Jack Dorsey and Facebook's Mark Zuckerberg

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:32.710
embraced the concept of a neutral public square.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:36.820
We do not want to become the arbiters of truth.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.710
The shift from digital commons

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:43.170
to actively curated newsfeed was underway long before the election.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:46.820
In October of 2020, Facebook deranked and Twitter blocked

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.750
the sharing of a New York post story,

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.180
claiming that Joe Biden met with an executive

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:54.890
at a Ukrainian gas company where his son held a board seat.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:57.080
Twitter also blocked the nation's oldest newspaper

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.000
from using its account for more than two weeks.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.870
When the New York Times' Kara Swisher,

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:07.828
grilled Parler CEO John Matze about Parler's role in inciting the Capitol breach,

00:03:07.828 --> 00:03:10.094
he defended its hands off approach.

00:03:10.094 --> 00:03:11.670
If it was organized on your site,

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.829
what should happen on your site?

00:03:14.829 --> 00:03:17.590
If it was illegally organized

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.400
and against the law and what they were doing,

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.660
they would've gotten it taken down,

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.980
but I don't feel responsible for any of this

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.210
and neither should the platform,

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:26.420
considering we're a neutral town square.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:29.780
The handful of companies that own the dominant share of social media

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:33.020
and the underlying infrastructure of the internet disagree,

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.760
and have made it increasingly difficult for Parler to operate,

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:40.200
but the most dangerous threat isn't coming from Silicon Valley.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.630
To get what they want from tech CEOs,

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:44.620
both Republicans and Democrats,

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.700
have regularly threatened to strip away

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:50.389
the liability protections provided by section 230

00:03:50.389 --> 00:03:52.840
of the Communications and Decency Act,

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.510
which is known as the internet's First Amendment.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.700
Through the effect of section 230

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.040
a special immunity from liability that nobody else gets.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.930
Congress has given big tech in effect, a subsidy.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.960
That's a pretty foundational law, of the modern network of internet.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:09.860
Exactly right.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.302
And it should be revoked.

00:04:12.302 --> 00:04:14.690
Democrats want to leverage section 230

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.388
to force them to weed out misinformation,

00:04:17.388 --> 00:04:19.870
which they falsely imagined can be sorted out

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.077
by panels of accredited experts

00:04:22.077 --> 00:04:23.710
or finely tuned algorithms.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.150
Republicans have threatened to repeal 230

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:29.200
unless platforms commit to viewpoint neutrality

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.450
a standard which Stanford technologist,

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.650
Daphne Keller, says is impossible to uphold.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.520
I don't even know what being neutral would mean.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.390
Would it mean allowing every single thing

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:42.970
to be uploaded and just showing it in chronological order?

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:46.150
Can you be neutral if you have search features?

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:53.000
Can you be neutral if you allow people to mute things?

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:56.080
I think a truly neutral meaning,

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.380
showing everything that is legal,

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:02.280
social media platform would be full of content

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.140
that most users don't want to see.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:10.930
President-elect Biden is making a public push for a new domestic terrorism law

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.170
and red flag laws,

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.280
which would make it easier for federal agents

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.697
to seize firearms based on a user's online posts.

00:05:17.697 --> 00:05:20.308
Perhaps Americans way of thinking about free speech,

00:05:20.308 --> 00:05:22.200
is not the best way,

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.927
wrote Emily Bazelon in the New York Times magazine.

00:05:24.927 --> 00:05:27.380
At the very least, we should understand

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.060
that it isn't the only way.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:31.200
And that European speech regulations

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.040
have created better conditions for their citizenry

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.590
to sort out what's true from what's not

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:38.150
and to make informed decisions

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.710
about what they want. their societies to be.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:45.000
But in the EU, these regulations have created unintended consequences

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.330
of flagging content that's disturbing,

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.210
yet vital to the public interest.

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:51.960
Such as an archive of Syrian war crimes,

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:54.310
wrongly flagged as terrorist content

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.890
under the EU guidelines.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:56.780
Right now,

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:01.660
we don't have any clear information telling us that,

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:05.340
taking down all of these videos really is making us safer.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:06.660
In fact, a lot of people,

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.270
who are expert researchers on security,

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:13.910
are concerned that this will effectively drive more people

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:16.518
into darker corners of the internet,

00:06:16.518 --> 00:06:20.060
into echo chambers where they only ever hear

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.300
from people who agree with a violent agenda.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.650
What do you think when people are saying

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.540
it's time for civil war,

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:27.850
I'm bringing my guns to Washington/

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:30.350
You think you just let them say that?

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.840
Well, if it was up to me, we wouldn't be in this situation

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:35.549
where two sides hate each other this much—I get it, but then here we find ourselves.

00:06:35.549 --> 00:06:37.070
Whether or not it's Parler,

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.910
it's Twitter, it's Facebook, it's Google,

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.549
it's Telegram, WhatsApp, whatever it might be,

00:06:41.549 --> 00:06:44.500
you can't stop people and change their opinions by force,

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.580
by censoring them.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.630
They'll just go somewhere else and do it.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.470
A study from social psychologist Richard Rogers

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:53.400
found that a robust network of deplatform figures

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:58.010
has already emerged over the past several years on encrypted apps like Telegram,

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:00.708
the preferred platform for pro-democracy activists

00:07:00.708 --> 00:07:04.210
in Hong Kong, trying to avoid Chinese censorship.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:08.350
A transition to a new, more decentralized and private web

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:11.940
may be accelerating as privacy centric DuckDuckGo

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:14.410
has experienced significant growth in search

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:15.840
as a Google alternative.

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.990
And the encrypted messaging app Signal saw a big bump

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:22.070
after Elon Musk encouraged the masses to install it.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:25.400
With a crackdown in progress and likely to intensify,

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:27.680
once a new Congress and president take office,

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:28.780
we should focus instead

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:31.720
on enhancing encrypted communication platforms

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.730
that make online speech harder to control

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:36.800
and resisting law enforcement efforts

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:41.060
to weaken vital tools like end to end encryption.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.000
There's a lot that still needs building

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.500
to create an alternative digital commons

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.450
but it can be accomplished.

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:50.590
Communicating freely might take more work in the future

00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:53.080
and your favorite politician might get banned

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.630
or your favorite app taken out of the store.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.920
But in this cat and mouse game,

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:00.090
the mice far outnumber of the cats.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:02.050
That said in the short term,

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:04.420
the decision-makers at Twitter and Facebook

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:06.820
may want to consider that repression tends

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.470
to have the unfortunate effect

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:10.250
of pushing legitimate dissidence

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:14.350
and dangerous unsavory extremists into the same channels.

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:16.130
Sigmund Freud theorized that

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:18.890
when thoughts or experiences are repressed,

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:23.160
they inevitably resurface in more deranged and damaging forms.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.240
When our dominant communication platforms,

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:28.240
seek to repress widely held beliefs and opinions,

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:31.410
those beliefs and opinions aren't likely to simply disappear

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:34.610
but rather re-emerge elsewhere in less visible forums,

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:36.490
where they'll face less scrutiny.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:38.470
The next few years may be ugly

00:08:38.470 --> 00:08:41.530
but silencing dissenters will ultimately fail.

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:43.650
Information wants to be free

00:08:43.650 --> 00:08:45.817
as Stewart Brand famously quipped,

00:08:45.817 --> 00:08:48.150
The great repression will almost certainly

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:50.230
have unintended consequences,

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:51.947
but it can't last forever.

